2:1 Multiplexer

Description

A 2:1 Multiplexer (MUX) is a digital circuit that selects one of two input signals and sends the selected input to the output based on the select line.

Inputs

- I0 – Input 0
- I1 – Input 1
- S – Select line

Output

- Y – Selected output

Boolean Expression

Y = (~S & I0) | (S & I1)

Working

- When S = 0, the output Y follows I0.
- When S = 1, the output Y follows I1.

Truth Table

S| Y
0| I0
1| I1

Language

Verilog HDL

